{"name":"Microchip","hex":"#babcc0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"microchip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An integrated circuit.\nA microprocessor.","A microprocessor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fit (an animal) with a microchip.","To cause microscopic chips (abrasions) in a material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microchip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Microchip (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"David Linus Lieberman is a fictional character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. He was an ally of The Punisher for many years and assisted the Punisher by building weapons, supplying technology, hacking into computers, and providing friendship. Microchip gradually evolved from the Punisher's friend to a bitter enemy after their final falling out."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6d/Microchip%28comics%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microchip_(comics)","wikidata":"Q978786"},{"title":"Integrated circuit","blocks":[{"text":"An integrated circuit (IC), also known as a microchip or simply chip, is a compact assembly of electronic circuits formed from various electronic components, such as transistors, resistors, and capacitors, and their interconnections. These components are fabricated onto a thin, flat piece (\"chip\") of semiconductor material, most commonly silicon. Integrated circuits are integral to a wide variety of electronic devices performing functions such as data processing, control, and storage. They have transformed the field of electronics by enabling device miniaturization, improving performance, and reducing cost."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/EPROM_Microchip_SuperMacro.jpg/330px-EPROM_Microchip_SuperMacro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_circuit","wikidata":"Q80831"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/62/Ebon_Moss-Bachrach_as_Micro.jpeg/330px-Ebon_Moss-Bachrach_as_Micro.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/62/Ebon_Moss-Bachrach_as_Micro.jpeg/330px-Ebon_Moss-Bachrach_as_Micro.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ebon Moss-Bachrach as Micro in the television series The Punisher","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEbon_Moss-Bachrach_as_Micro.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/NXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_%28Colour_Corrected%29.jpg/500px-NXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_%28Colour_Corrected%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/NXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_%28Colour_Corrected%29.jpg/1280px-NXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_%28Colour_Corrected%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/NXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_%28Colour_Corrected%29.jpg/500px-NXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_%28Colour_Corrected%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A microscope image of an integrated circuit die used to control LCDs. The pinouts are the dark circles surrounding the integrated circuit.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANXP_PCF8577C_LCD_driver_with_I%C2%B2C_(Colour_Corrected).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/42/Kilby_solid_circuit.jpg/330px-Kilby_solid_circuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/42/Kilby_solid_circuit.jpg/330px-Kilby_solid_circuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wi